{
  "schema": 1,
  "role": "Reviewed intent. Human-edited. Lists every snow texture to generate.",
  "conventions": {
    "lengthAxis": "Y",
    "upAxis": "+Z",
    "flipV": false,
    "evidence": "Verified against MSR788_Rifle: the muzzle attachment offset Y=0.4968 equals the mesh maximum Y=0.4966, the scope attachment sits at Z=+0.0491 above the bore at Z=+0.0308, and a textured side render is upright only with +Z up and V used directly.",
    "warning": "Y=length holds across every vanilla firearm mesh sampled, but no cheap geometric test reliably recovers the up SIGN: 'up area exceeds down area' fails on 1911_Pistol and D_E_Pistol, and 'centroid below mid-height' fails on every rifle. Each asset therefore carries an explicit axis and must be confirmed by looking at a render before its recipe is frozen.",
    "stageProgression": "noiseBase and edgeSoftness are IDENTICAL across the stages of one weapon, on purpose. The mask keeps one noise field and only lowers the threshold, so each stage's snow is a superset of the previous stage's. Re-rolling the field per stage would make snow appear in different places between stages, which reads in game as snow teleporting when a threshold is crossed. Only targetUpCoverage, flankCoverage and flankMaxAlpha vary.",
    "wiring": "Model blocks and EW_Profiles.lua are generated by tools/generate_mod_wiring.js from this spec plus the vanilla ModelScript attachments. vanillaModel names the ModelScript to copy attachments from; modelName is the EW model that the profile selects for that stage.",
    "saturation": "targetUpCoverage never reaches 1.0. Once the up-facing region of a UV island is fully covered, the visible snow edge is no longer the mask boundary but the edge of the geometry, and on a cylinder like a barrel or handguard that edge is a straight line by definition. Keeping a margin of holes at every stage is what makes the transition read as organic. Stage 4 is 'heavily snowed with gaps', not 'buried'."
  },
